    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Some of the land along Kenai Fjords coastline is owned by the Port Graham Corporation, an Alaska Native Corporation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/kefj/planyourvisit/port-graham-corporation-lands.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Formed under the 1971 Alaska Native Settlement Act, the Port Graham Corporation represents Sugpiaq people on the Kenai Peninsula's Cook Inlet coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/kefj/planyourvisit/port-graham-corporation-lands.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Port Graham Corporation partners with Kenai Fjords National Park to protect the region's ecological and cultural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/kefj/planyourvisit/port-graham-corporation-lands.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Accessing private Port Graham Corporation lands requires a permit, though some easement areas allow up to 24 hours of use without one.",
